# Zone identity (M4 polish): forest edge - pines (two variants) mixed with round trees, fallen logs, and a wooden gateway (non-solid 2 x 1 arch) where the
# path enters the forest (j = 2).
# Ruta 2 (Route 2): Ciudad Nodo (south, j = 31) to the Bosque Umbrio (north, j = 0). column = i, row = j. Winding path, tall-grass
# patches with the wild table, two one-way ledge rows facing south (hop SW = +j; the gaps keep the route two-way), a salve on the
# ground in the west pocket, and a junior explorer looking across the path (range 4: his line of sight (-1,+1) crosses both path columns).
@map ruta_2
@size 20 32
@interior no
@area ruta_2
@bg 0
@fill grass
@spawn south 10 30 N           # arriving from Ciudad Nodo
@spawn north 10 1 S            # arriving from the Bosque Umbrio
@spawn cave 18 25 NW           # C3: coming out of the Cueva Excavadora (the pocket is closed by a cuttable bush)
@encounters grass rate=25      # Route 2 rate; the forest-edge bugs join the Route 1 pair
  muncrit 3 5 40
  flitter 3 5 35
  grubbit 3 5 15
  stingle 3 5 10
@end
# Open ground (contract 63, transit road): a step onto plain ground (not tall grass, water, a door, a ledge, an arrow floor) rolls this table when rand8 < 2 (2/256 per step).
@open_rate 2
# Roaming wild creatures (contract 55, rollout in 63): 2 creatures of this table wander the open ground (not the tall grass); touching one starts that wild battle.
@roam 2 table=grass period=1800
@legend
  .  tile=grass
  =  tile=path
  g  tile=tall_grass
  T  object=tree              # round trees (a third of the wall)
  P  object=pine              # pines (variants pine_a / pine_b): the forest edge
  l  object=log               # fallen log
  A  tile=path object=arch    # wooden gateway (2 x 1) across the 2-wide path: free to walk through, the posts stand on its edges
  r  object=rock
  v  ledge=SW
  u  tile=path
  d  tile=path
  S  tile=grass object=sign interact=look text=ruta2.sign
  i  item=salve
  b  cut=yes                  # C3: the cuttable bush that closes the cave's pocket
  W  tile=grass object=hole   # C3: the cave mouth (the Cueva Excavadora, Cave south entrance)
  x  npc=explorador id=scout face=W trainer=explorador_r2 range=4 text=tr.explorador_r2.pre after=tr.explorador_r2.after
  Q  tile=grass npc=ayudante id=aide face=W script=aide   # C4a: Profesora Lin's aide at the Nodo end (the Linterna for 10 caught species)
  H  tile=grass hidden=antidote   # hidden (contract 80, hidden items)
@grid
  TPPPTPPPTuuPTPPPTPPP
  PPPTPPPT.==.PPPTPPPT
  PP.....P.AA.ggggg.TP
  P.gggggPP==.ggggg..P
  T.ggggg..==........P
  P.ggggg..==...l.r..T
  P.ggggg..==..ggggg.P
  P........==.lggggg.P
  TPPPl....==.TgggggPP
  PP..P...P==..gggggPT
  P.......P==........P
  Pvvvvvvv.==.vvvvvvvP
  T........==P.......P
  PPi..rPT.==....TPP.T
  PP..r...P==.......TP
  PT.......==...x..TPP
  THgggggg.==.....TPPP
  P.gggggg.===....PPPT
  P.gggggg..==.PT...TP
  P.ggggggl.==.......P
  T.gggggg..==...ggggP
  P.......P.==...ggggT
  PP.PPP.PP.==...ggggP
  P.........==r..ggggP
  Tvvvvvvvv.==.vvvvPPP
  P.........==.....b.W
  P.gggggr.===.....PTP
  P.gggggl.==..ggggg.P
  T.ggggg..==..ggggg.P
  PPggggg.S==Q.ggggg.T
  PPT......==..gggggTP
  PTPPPTPPPddPPTPPPTPP
@warp u -> bosque_umbrio spawn=south
@warp d -> ciudad_nodo spawn=north
@warp W -> cueva_excavadora spawn=ruta2
# C4a (contract 39): Profesora Lin's aide. With at least 10 species CAUGHT in the Registro he gives the LINTERNA module (flag 89 = `setf mod_linterna`,
# the bracelet module that lights the dark tunnel); with fewer he says how many are still missing (`caught_ge` leaves the missing number in {v2}).
@var c4_ok 5
@script aide npc
    npc_face_hero aide
    jf mod_linterna said
    say ruta2.aide.hi
    caught_ge c4_ok 10
    jv c4_ok 1 give
    say ruta2.aide.more
    end
  give:
    say ruta2.aide.give
    setf mod_linterna
    sfx item
    say ruta2.aide.got
    say ruta2.aide.about
    end
  said:
    say ruta2.aide.after
@end
